# --- caller evidence (post-fix kernel; the line names its caller) -----
# The kernel's loud-unimplemented line now prints the current proc's pid
# and name (x86_64/src/syscall.rs). Serial capture of the fixed TCG run:
syscall 10 unimplemented (pid 1 boot)
syscall 10 unimplemented (pid 1 init)

# syscall 10 = FAUTH (Harvey sys/src/libc/9syscall/sys.h). The callers are
# Harvey's UNCHANGED boot path: boot(8)'s nsinit calls fauth(fd, rp) on the
# connected root fd and tolerates -1 (sys/src/9/boot/boot.c:148); init's
# mount path calls fauth the same way. FAUTH is loud-None by design
# (D-02's measured-set rule), so there is no new kernel gap to open here.
# The narrow fix is the profile registration in xtask/src/main.rs:
#   * q35churnshell rides the q35shell chain stages (PCI discovery ->
#     NIC bind -> module/paqfs -> exec entry -> Q35ChainBoot -> init
#     handoff -> `% ` prompt), because dev_churn + dev_bootchain keeps
#     the normal boot chain (the churn driver never runs);
#   * the negative scan exempts exactly `syscall 10 unimplemented` for
#     that profile (the same one-line exemption net/netip/q35shell/q35cpu
#     carry), and any other unimplemented syscall still fails
#     (xtask test `negative_scan_exempts_boot_fauth_only`).

# --- fixed run ---------------------------------------------------------
# `cargo xtask boot-test --arch x86-64 --config q35churnshell --accel tcg
#  --cpu qemu64`
# (--cpu qemu64: the profile's TOML cpu is `host`, which QEMU TCG rejects;
#  the Linux CI uses the same explicit qemu64. grub-mkrescue is bridged to
#  a linux/amd64 container because the darwin devshell has no grub2.)
boot-test: PASS -- SeaBIOS -> GRUB2 -> mb2 kernel + chain-module boot: banner, memory facts, discovery, the NIC bind, the module-tag/paqfs mount notes, the exec-entry note, then the REAL boot(8)→init→rc chain's own ring-3 prints (paqfs/version handoffs, the init rc handoff) through to the interactive `% ` prompt, observed in order — XEXEC-03 leg 2 (D-08's staged chain on the proven exec substrate; the composed Harvey-side gate is 14-07's)
